{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792832322,"nonce":"q0Xog13fly+i6lYc9VUSXHihqPU=","title":"Expose blinc_abi to Caribou as a plugin, beside the HashLink and Node adapters","message":"**Why**\nashui is to run on Caribou's gpu, window and xavi plugins (user, 2026-10-24). blinc_abi is the one native library ashui still reaches only as a HashLink HDLL. Caribou can load an HDLL for a Haxe program, but a plugin built with `caribou_abi::plugin!` is what every Caribou language reaches directly (Wren, Zyntax) and what a wasm program links, so blinc_abi should offer that form too. The HashLink build stays as it is.\n\n**Design**\nThe runtime-neutral cores already exist (owned graph/layout contexts, scene, text, bitmap, hit, css), shared with the Node adapter, and effects are host-run by id rather than by closure. A `caribou` feature (no libhl, `caribou_abi` only) adds one more thin adapter over them: `plugin!` declarations that name the same functions the HashLink exports have, over Caribou's carriers (Text for strings, buffers for bytes, handles as `Box\u003cT\u003e` classes, 64-bit node ids as i64). No logic is duplicated; if an operation exists only in the HashLink layer, it moves into the neutral core first.\n\n**Slices**\n1. Layout tree and nodes (tree, node, layout props): enough to build a tree and lay it out from a Caribou Haxe program.\n2. The reactive graph and host-run effects.\n3. The display list, text, fonts, svg, bitmap and hit testing.\n4. CSS (the compiled sheet and cascade).\n5. ashui's Haxe: under `-D ashui_caribou` the `ashui.core.externs.*` classes call the generated plugin classes instead of `@:hlNative(\"blinc_abi\")`.\n\n**Checks**\nThe 209 HashLink exports stay exactly as they are (cargo build --release --locked; export list compared). The same compiled scenes give pixel-identical images through the HashLink and Caribou adapters, as the Node adapter's check did.\n\n**Open**\nWhether wasm uses the plugin (statically linked) or the existing side module; which Caribou build and staging to test against (asked Caribou's session).","files":null}]}